From b2cda7ca206974fc593eef2790fa1f9daa493260 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elliotttate <elliotttate@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 18:15:50 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Aurora: in-between frames for 60 FPS, and an FPS counter

Wind Waker's logic runs at 30 steps a second. With in-between frames on, the
render worker keeps each finished frame, encodes its passes a second time with
every draw's transforms blended halfway toward the same draw in the previous
frame, presents that, and presents the kept frame half a game frame later:
60 frames a second of real geometry (depth, lighting and the HUD exact) with
the game's logic unchanged.

- frame_interp.*: draws are keyed by their FIFO payload (or shape and texture
  for direct positions) and matched occurrence-first; a pair must be plausibly
  one object a frame apart (skinned draws check the matrix slots they use),
  and 40 percent implausible is a camera cut. Copies of one model (grass,
  bushes, trees), culled one by one, are matched by the camera's motion, which
  the draws with a unique key vote for; a copy that comes into view is blended
  from where that motion carries it from.
- Blended blocks go to their own 32 MB uniform area and bind group.
- aurora_set_frame_interpolation / DOL_AURORA_FRAME_INTERP, debug logging,
  tracing and dumps (DOL_AURORA_FRAME_INTERP_*); a unit test.
- aurora_set_fps_overlay / DOL_AURORA_SHOW_FPS: "60 FPS (game 30)" at the top
  of the window.

BlueWake's patches/recompcore/0098.
